            <ArticleTitle>Stenting coronary trifurcation lesions: is &quot;ménage à trois&quot; the solution?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>372-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Percutaneous treatment of coronary stenoses involving important side branches remains a challenge to the interventionist. We describe two cases of stent deployment in coronary trifurcation lesions. Triple kissing balloon inflation appears important for achieving an optimal angiographic and clinical result.</AbstractText>
